 the familiar operation semantics while exposing batching as a separate,
 explicit scheduling API.
 
+## Schedule general GPU pipelines
+
+`submit(pipeline_op)` accepts one instance carrying its input image and
+operation. Python's `ImageBatch.PipelineOp(image, operation)` binds an image
+to a builder using normal `PIL` methods, or an operation parameter object.
+Rust's `PipelineOpInstance::new(image, operation)` binds an image to a
+normalized `PipelineOp` descriptor. The GPU registry determines support; unsupported GPU operations are
+rejected during `submit`, before the queue or result metadata is changed.
+
+```python
+from PIL import Image, ImageBatch
+
+batch = ImageBatch.BatchExecutor(queue=True, backend="gpu")
+resize = ImageBatch.PipelineOp(
+    image_a,
+    lambda image: image.resize((320, 240), Image.Resampling.NEAREST)
+)
+rotate = ImageBatch.PipelineOp(
+    image_b,
+    lambda image: image.transpose(Image.Transpose.ROTATE_90)
+)
+batch.submit(resize)
+batch.submit(rotate)
+result_a, result_b = batch.join()
+```
+
+```rust
+use pillow_rs::{Backend, BatchExecutor, Image, PipelineOp, PipelineOpInstance, ResampleFilter};
+
+let source = Image::new(640, 480, "RGB", (30, 60, 90, 255))?;
+let mut batch = BatchExecutor::new(true, Some(Backend::Gpu));
+let resize = PipelineOpInstance::new(source, PipelineOp::Resize {
+    w: 320,
+    h: 240,
+    filter: ResampleFilter::Nearest,
+});
+batch.submit(resize)?;
+let results = batch.join()?;
+# Ok::<(), pillow_rs::PilError>(())
+```
+
+Creating an instance binds the input without executing its operation.
+The builder runs during `submit` to normalize descriptors. It retains the
+ordinary PIL method behavior, including reads that may materialize a preceding
+stage. Submission validates the constructed descriptors before enqueueing.
+`join()` executes accepted pipelines using
+its existing GPU dispatch plan and returns results in submission order. Each
+image retains independent boundaries, statistics, and auxiliary operands;
+histograms from separate images are never combined. With `queue=False`, the
+submitted pipeline completes before `submit` returns.
+
+General submission requires GPU as the executor's selected backend. A plain
+image with no pipeline operations raises `ValueError`; an unsupported descriptor
+raises `NotImplementedError` at submission. Known native-mode restrictions,
+including palette/YCbCr blur, are also rejected before enqueueing. The validator
+uses available loaded, palette, header, and lazy-pipeline metadata without
+decoding images just to check support.
+Content-dependent exactness and device-resource restrictions can reject a job
+during execution. This route
+raises an error when native GPU execution is unavailable, including auxiliary
+image pipelines. It does not silently substitute CPU work. A failed `join`
+drains the current queue; the executor can accept a new batch afterward.
+Drawing and noise paths that generate a full result on the host and then copy
+it through a GPU shader are rejected during submission. Autocontrast uses the existing GPU histogram and
+remap passes in this route, avoiding the ordinary host-histogram shortcut.
+
+Compatible single operations reuse the existing image grouping kernels.
+The same native GPU policy covers grouping, auxiliary input preparation, and
+individual jobs; a previously CPU-locked lazy operand is recursively locked to
+GPU before it is evaluated.
+Other pipelines run separate per-image GPU plans; arbitrary pipelines are not
+combined into one device submission. Both routes use the same `submit` API.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    A[PipelineOp instance: input + operation] --> B[submit: validate GPU support]
+    B --> C[Compatible image groups]
+    B --> D[Independent pipeline plans]
+    C --> F[join]
+    D --> F
+    F --> G[Existing GPU dispatch plans]
+    G --> H[Results in submission order]
+```
+
+## Combine compatible image jobs
+
